OL,3,GNEWSATenants could be offered upgrades
OL,4,Ato downsize
OL,5,
OL,6,FCroydon Council tenants who agree to
OL,7,Fmove from homes with more space than
OL,8,Fthey need could be offered new
OL,9,Fkitchens, bathrooms and full
OL,10,Fredecoration under a new housing
OL,11,Fscheme.
OL,13,FThe pilot, which is expected to launch
OL,14,Fat the end of October, is aimed at
OL,15,Ffreeing up family-sized properties as
OL,16,Fmore than 8,500 households wait for
OL,17,Fsuitable accommodation in the borough.
OL,19,FMore than 1,000 council properties are
OL,20,Fcurrently classed as under-occupied,
OL,21,Faccounting for about 8.5% of Croydon's
OL,22,Fhousing stock.
OL,23,APub: 09-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
